+## 2026-11-01: no section edit links for headings of included wiki pages (#44623)
+
+What changed: macros can declare `:sections => true` (`lib/redmine/wiki_formatting/macros.rb`); only `collapse` does. When `textilizable` renders with `:edit_section_links`, `inject_macros` replaces the output of every other macro (for example `include`) with a placeholder, and `parse_sections` puts the output back after it has numbered the headings (`app/helpers/application_helper.rb`). Included headings are still rendered with anchors, but get no edit link and do not shift the section numbers. Tests: `test_section_edit_links_with_include_macro` (helper) and two macro registration tests (unit). `bin/harness check` passes (6065 tests, 0 failures).
+
+What I learned: section numbers for editing come from the page source (`Redmine::WikiFormatting::SectionHelper#get_section`), where `{{include}}` is one line and the `collapse` block text is part of the source. So the rendered numbering must count `collapse` headings and ignore `include` headings. `bin/rails test` needs the Homebrew Ruby on PATH on macOS; `bin/harness` does this itself, but plain `bin/rails` uses the system Ruby 2.6 and fails with a bundler error.
+
+What is left: plugin macros that render text from the page source (like `collapse`) must add `:sections => true`, or their headings lose the edit links. This is a behavior change for plugins.
